{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc '\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" response items > commands/response-items.stdout 2> commands/response-items.stderr; echo $? > commands/response-items.exit; cat commands/response-items.stdout; cat commands/response-items.stderr; python - <<'\"'PY'\nimport json,os,hashlib\nfor base in [os.path.dirname(os.environ['STAMPED_DELIVERY_MANIFEST']),os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.environ['STAMPED_DELIVERY_MANIFEST']))]:\n p=os.path.join(base,'judge-target.json')\n if os.path.exists(p):\n  x=json.load(open(p)); print('REFLIMITS',p, x.get('reference_limits')); print('keys',x.keys())\nm=json.load(open(os.environ['STAMPED_DELIVERY_MANIFEST'])); print('CAPTURE',os.environ['STAMPED_WORKER_STOP_RECEIPT']); print('HEAD',m['head_commit']); print('entries',len(m['entries']));\nby={e['path']:e for e in m['entries']}\nfor p in ['content/workspace/report.md','content/workspace/analysis/group_analysis.py','content/workspace/results/summary.json','content/workspace/results/input_qc.csv','content/workspace/results/fwe_clusters.csv','content/workspace/results/vmPFC_mask_definition.txt','content/workspace/input/participants.tsv','content/workspace/input/upstream-methods.md']:\n e=by.get(p); print(p, (e or {}).get('sha256'), (e or {}).get('size'), (e or {}).get('kind'))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc '\"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" response items > commands/response-items.stdout 2> commands/response-items.stderr; echo $? > commands/response-items.exit; cat commands/response-items.stdout; cat commands/response-items.stderr; python - <<'\"'PY'\nimport json,os,hashlib\nfor base in [os.path.dirname(os.environ['STAMPED_DELIVERY_MANIFEST']),os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.environ['STAMPED_DELIVERY_MANIFEST']))]:\n p=os.path.join(base,'judge-target.json')\n if os.path.exists(p):\n  x=json.load(open(p)); print('REFLIMITS',p, x.get('reference_limits')); print('keys',x.keys())\nm=json.load(open(os.environ['STAMPED_DELIVERY_MANIFEST'])); print('CAPTURE',os.environ['STAMPED_WORKER_STOP_RECEIPT']); print('HEAD',m['head_commit']); print('entries',len(m['entries']));\nby={e['path']:e for e in m['entries']}\nfor p in ['content/workspace/report.md','content/workspace/analysis/group_analysis.py','content/workspace/results/summary.json','content/workspace/results/input_qc.csv','content/workspace/results/fwe_clusters.csv','content/workspace/results/vmPFC_mask_definition.txt','content/workspace/input/participants.tsv','content/workspace/input/upstream-methods.md']:\n e=by.get(p); print(p, (e or {}).get('sha256'), (e or {}).get('size'), (e or {}).get('kind'))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"stamped-checklist:must/001\tmust\tS.1\tAre all files and directories nested under a common root?\nstamped-checklist:must/002\tmust\tS.1\tAre datasets included, linked, or referenced reachable from the code and environment specifications without crossing the boundary of a common root?\nstamped-checklist:must/003\tmust\tS.1\tIs external software included in the environment or linked as submodules within the project boundary?\nstamped-checklist:must/004\tmust\tT.1,T.3,T.5\tAre version control systems such as `Git` used for code, text, documentation, and configuration files?\nstamped-checklist:must/005\tmust\tT.1,T.3,T.5\tAre version control systems such as `git-annex`, DataLad, or `Git` LFS used for large binary data?\nstamped-checklist:must/006\tmust\tT.1,T.3,T.5\tAre the exact environment specifications used to generate a set of results included in the provenance records to link computational actions to particular environments?\nstamped-checklist:must/007\tmust\tA.1\tIs a `README.md` or `Makefile` included with instructions for installation and usage?\nstamped-checklist:must/008\tmust\tA.1\tIs there a clear starting point for users to start reproducing results (e.g., a main script, a workflow definition, or a container image)?\nstamped-checklist:must/009\tmust\tP.1\tAre relative paths used in scripts, avoiding hardcoded or system-specific paths like `C:\\Users\\...` or `/home/user/...`?\nstamped-checklist:must/010\tmust\tP.1\tAre all software dependencies included in the environment specification, rather than relying on pre-installed tools?\nstamped-checklist:must/011\tmust\tP.1\tHave all assumptions about the host system's configuration been documented (e.g., specific OS versions, required system libraries, or environment variables)?\nstamped-checklist:must/012\tmust\tP.2\tIs there a clear list of system requirements and dependencies documented in the README or environment specifications?\nstamped-checklist:must/013\tmust\tP.3\tAre environment specifications (e.g., Dockerfiles, `pyproject.toml`, `package.json`) included in the version control system alongside code and data?\nstamped-checklist:must/014\tmust\tP.3\tIs there a process for updating environment specifications when dependencies change, and are these updates tracked in version control?\nstamped-checklist:must/015\tmust\tD.1\tAre environment specifications (e.g., container digests, frozen package manifests) included to ensure others can attempt to exactly replicate the environment?\nstamped-checklist:must/016\tmust\tD.1\tAre environment specifications shared in a way that others can access and use them (e.g., published container images, archived environment files)?\nstamped-checklist:must/017\tmust\tD.1\tIs there documentation on how to obtain and use the environment specifications for reproduction?\nstamped-checklist:should/001\tshould\tT.2\tIs a common version control system (e.g., `Git`, DVC, `git-annex`, or DataLad) used across all components?\nstamped-checklist:should/002\tshould\tA.2\tIs the workflow tested regularly to ensure instructions remain accurate?\nstamped-checklist:should/003\tshould\tM.1\tAre raw data, processed data, code, and environment definitions separated into distinct modules?\nstamped-checklist:should/009\tshould\tM.4\tAre restricted data or software kept in their own modules?\nstamped-checklist:should/004\tshould\tE.1\tIs the pipeline tested in a fresh container, batch job, clean virtual machine, or cloud-based instance?\nstamped-checklist:should/005\tshould\tE.1\tDoes the workflow spawn disposable environments for each execution, allowing for isolation of runs?\nstamped-checklist:should/006\tshould\tD.2\tAre the exact environment specifications used to generate a specific set of results regularly tested to ensure they can be reconstituted as intended?\nstamped-checklist:should/007\tshould\tD.2\tAre environment artifacts archived within the research object where possible (e.g., executable binaries, container images)?\nstamped-checklist:should/008\tshould\tD.2\tIs there a process for updating environment specifications when dependencies change, and are these updates tracked in version control?\nstamped-checklist:may/001\tmay\tM.2\tAre external datasets or software dependencies included as submodules or linked as submodules?\nstamped-checklist:may/002\tmay\tM.2\tIs the modular structure documented to clarify how components relate and can be recombined?\nstamped-checklist:may/003\tmay\tM.2\tAre modular boundaries defined in a way that allows independent updates without breaking the overall workflow?\nstamped-checklist:may/004\tmay\tM.2\tIs there a clear mechanism for composing modules together (e.g., `git` submodules, or container orchestration)?\nstamped-checklist:may/005\tmay\tM.2\tIs there documentation or tooling to support users in understanding and navigating the modular structure?\n✔ The default environment has been installed.\nCAPTURE /Users/johnlee/.local/state/stamped-in-practice/narps-neutral-v1/assessment-series/narps-neutral-r1-operational-v4/judgments/narps-neutral-r1-15-j01/attempt-01/worker-end-state.json\nHEAD d857ab1302d13cb660a7a044af07141f44bfa9ba\nentries 1143\ncontent/workspace/report.md f6804e630acad03d64a4503451751d62b37849c026678a234775f9414737a726 6785 file\ncontent/workspace/analysis/group_analysis.py 5e4224df7b7a4c1e5d4fb47271604e908bc4313685322d29710f1dfafec8ddfb 11886 file\ncontent/workspace/results/summary.json df9593e4a9df67cdf50fd355c3ca8e34734ccafc95c78ec67366f79ad5d39f9a 1281 file\ncontent/workspace/results/input_qc.csv f99f9807fa8e53b31e1f7252c037526ec6152a62648f07ae41ac479ee128e124 9546 file\ncontent/workspace/results/fwe_clusters.csv a1fce2adef2b3ca9a3f950f5f04e91810891794816ca8e9cb1c6f4f6c4ffd94f 428 file\ncontent/workspace/results/vmPFC_mask_definition.txt 599b0c61062912e2ab55f43f408437f822302a446e38ca5e401b5aa9301133e0 512 file\ncontent/workspace/input/participants.tsv faca815bcb042144bdb8dcff915f45de0d27650f60416ed76a5a72557341abbf 1706 file\ncontent/workspace/input/upstream-methods.md 508d832c8787ed8303c3de101c2c76f40a3aa5dec53e6993dc2a49c4b7bcf90b 1342 file\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
