{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'for a in template stamp set validate encode table; do \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" response \"$a\" --help; done;'","aggregated_output":"✔ The default environment has been installed.\nusage: encode_response.py template [-h] [-o OUTPUT]\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help           show this help message and exit\n  -o, --output OUTPUT\n✔ The default environment has been installed.\nusage: encode_response.py stamp [-h] [--harness HARNESS] [--model MODEL]\n                                [--scope SCOPE]\n                                [--kind {dataset,component,study,skill}]\n                                [--dependency DEPENDENCY] [--capture CAPTURE]\n                                response\n\npositional arguments:\n  response\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --harness HARNESS     e.g. \"claude-code (subagent)\"\n  --model MODEL\n  --scope SCOPE         what this assessment did and did not cover\n  --kind {dataset,component,study,skill}\n                        the object's kind (see references/project-kinds.md)\n  --dependency DEPENDENCY\n                        e.g. \"stamped-conventions@0.1.0\"; repeatable\n  --capture CAPTURE     hash a retained delivery manifest/archive; preserve\n                        any recorded Git commit\n✔ The default environment has been installed.\nusage: encode_response.py set [-h] --item ITEM\n                              --status {met,not-applicable,not-checked,partial,unmet}\n                              --reason REASON [--source SOURCE]\n                              [--evidence EVIDENCE] [--flag FLAGS]\n                              [--drop-evidence]\n                              response\n\npositional arguments:\n  response\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --item ITEM           item id, with or without the 'stamped-checklist:'\n                        prefix\n  --status {met,not-applicable,not-checked,partial,unmet}\n  --reason REASON\n  --source SOURCE       probe:<name>, judgement, probe:<name>+judgement,\n                        human:web-app\n  --evidence EVIDENCE   uri, or uri=description; repeatable\n  --flag FLAGS\n  --drop-evidence       clear the evidence already on this item (by default it\n                        is kept when --evidence is not given)\n✔ The default environment has been installed.\nusage: encode_response.py validate [-h] response\n\npositional arguments:\n  response\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help  show this help message and exit\n✔ The default environment has been installed.\nusage: encode_response.py encode [-h] [--base-url BASE_URL] [--allow-invalid]\n                                 response\n\npositional arguments:\n  response\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help           show this help message and exit\n  --base-url BASE_URL\n  --allow-invalid      encode even if validation fails\n✔ The default environment has been installed.\nusage: encode_response.py table [-h] [-o OUTPUT] response\n\npositional arguments:\n  response\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help           show this help message and exit\n  -o, --output OUTPUT\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
