{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'python -m json.tool \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/results/summary.json\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/results/fwe_clusters.csv\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/results/vmPFC_participant_effects.csv\" | tail -5; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/results/vmPFC_mask_definition.txt\"; cat \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_TARGET/input/upstream-methods.md\"'","aggregated_output":"{\n    \"n_participants\": 54,\n    \"excluded_participants\": [],\n    \"mask_voxels\": 198029,\n    \"voxel_volume_mm3\": 9.600000381469727,\n    \"whole_brain_mask_volume_ml\": 1901.0784755420684,\n    \"permutations\": 10000,\n    \"seed\": 20261016,\n    \"one_sided\": true,\n    \"maxT_95_threshold\": 5.381128311157227,\n    \"whole_brain_fwe_significant_voxels\": 24,\n    \"vmPFC_mask_voxels\": 1821,\n    \"vmPFC_mask_volume_ml\": 17.48160171508789,\n    \"vmPFC_mean_effect\": -0.0005117690889164805,\n    \"vmPFC_95ci_t\": [\n        -0.02221120104246767,\n        0.02118766286463471\n    ],\n    \"vmPFC_dz\": -0.006437314679453736,\n    \"vmPFC_t\": -0.047304408835168524,\n    \"vmPFC_p_one_sided_uncorrected\": 0.5187757912614934,\n    \"vmPFC_fwe_significant_voxels\": 0,\n    \"top_voxel\": {\n        \"x\": -26.0,\n        \"y\": -102.0,\n        \"z\": -3.599997043609619,\n        \"mean_effect\": 0.11212667576209814,\n        \"t\": 6.617173246302241,\n        \"p_uncorrected\": 9.311564027968496e-09,\n        \"p_fwe_maxT\": 0.0005999400059994001,\n        \"vmPFC_operational_roi\": false\n    },\n    \"group_mean_effect_median_in_mask\": -0.00668044062115735,\n    \"participant_map_mean_median\": -0.008956247940659523,\n    \"participant_map_mean_range\": [\n        -0.1336822509765625,\n        0.10376109182834625\n    ],\n    \"age_mean\": 26.055555555555557,\n    \"age_sd\": 3.0493838948818466,\n    \"gender_counts\": {\n        \"F\": 30,\n        \"M\": 24\n    }\n}\ncluster,voxels_26_connected,volume_mm3,peak_x,peak_y,peak_z,peak_t,peak_mean_effect,peak_p_fwe_maxT\n1,17,163.20001220703125,-26.0,-102.0,-3.599997043609619,6.617173246302241,0.11212667576209814,0.0005999400059994001\n2,2,19.200000762939453,26.0,-98.0,-1.1999969482421875,5.760898732461179,0.10030006735986616,0.012398760123987601\n3,5,48.0,30.0,-94.0,-8.399997234344482,6.193402982181888,0.09332243645460242,0.0033996600339966003\nsub-115,-0.08299206\nsub-117,-0.14398889\nsub-119,0.011597838\nsub-121,-0.074323066\nsub-123,0.12322532\nHarvard-Oxford cortical max-probability atlas, threshold 25%, labels: Frontal Medial Cortex (25) restricted to z <= 30 mm, Subcallosal Cortex (27), and Frontal Orbital Cortex (33) restricted to |MNI x| <= 20 mm and z <= 30 mm restricted to |MNI x| <= 20 mm and z <= 30 mm; nearest-neighbour resampled to participant grid; intersected with common participant nonzero coverage. This is an operational anatomical localization mask, not a uniquely established vmPFC boundary. Whole-brain max-T inference is primary.\n# Fixed upstream analysis\n\nEach map is one participant's unthresholded gain-effect estimate from NARPS team AO86, averaged across four runs.\nThe 54 participants comprise the complete equal-indifference group in OpenNeuro ds001734 version 1.0.4.\nThese are effect estimates, not standardized test statistics or group results.\nMaps are reported in MNI152NLin2009cAsym space.\n\nAO86 used fMRIPrep outputs and nistats participant models.\nTheir reported gain regressor was mean-centered and variance-normalized before HRF convolution; its coefficients must not be interpreted as change per currency unit.\nResponse trials used response-time durations, with separate response-choice and gain modulators.\nNonresponse trials, motion terms, flagged volumes and drift terms were also modeled; runs were combined within participant.\nGain and loss used separate models, so the supplied gain effect is conditional on that modeling choice.\n\nThe reported upstream choices are fixed for this task.\nParticipant variance maps and a complete executable upstream pipeline are not supplied; account for these limits when choosing and interpreting group inference.\n`participants.tsv` retains the source group, age and gender columns.\n`sources.json` identifies each original image, its retrieved-byte checksum, the pinned cohort table and the original methods report.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"agent_message","text":"The scientific analysis is coherent on its stated scope: it tests positive effects with participant-level sign flips and whole-brain max-T FWE, then reports no corrected vmPFC voxels while treating the negative ROI average as descriptive. I found no declared dependency environment or usable worker access route, so I will mark replay not checked rather than run with an assessor-installed environment."}}
