{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\np='report.md'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('The supplied canonical and operational manifests report complete captures with no omissions or capture errors, the same captured HEAD, no external Git dependencies, and a workspace-resident \"'`.git` directory. The launcher verifies the operational copy against the canonical capture before and after assessment. No target content was intentionally changed; any annex keys database metadata writes made by inspection are excluded from scientific evidence. This does not claim logical database equivalence. No retained external pointer was followed.'\"', 'The supplied canonical and operational manifests report complete captures with no omissions or capture errors, the same captured HEAD, no external Git dependencies, and a workspace-resident \"'`.git` directory. `judge-target.json` has an empty `reference_limits` list. A final byte and link comparison found no non-permitted changes to the operational copy. Inspection changed only permitted regular-file annex metadata: `.git/annex/keysdb/db` changed from captured SHA-256 `f6f8fd7af99434db59fadc6da021051789c6aaa271ebf878c54dafc6c9fde5ca` to `233c0be3e02857e0fbf47b00b8a94de3e9126529bee41b2491286aef7372be80`; `db-shm` and `db-wal` were created. These are inspection-induced operational metadata and not worker evidence; logical database equivalence is not claimed. The launcher verifies the operational copy against the canonical capture before and after assessment. No retained external pointer was followed.'\"')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\n\\\"\"'$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" response table response.json -o response-table.md > commands/response-table.stdout 2> commands/response-table.stderr; echo $? > commands/response-table.exit; \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_RUNNER\" response validate response.json > commands/response-validate.stdout 2> commands/response-validate.stderr; echo $? > commands/response-validate.exit; cat commands/response-validate.stdout; cat commands/response-validate.stderr'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
