ommands/response-validate.stdout 2> commands/response-validate.stderr; echo $? > commands/response-validate.exit; cat commands/response-validate.stdout; cat commands/response-validate.stderr'","aggregated_output":"ok: 31 answers against checklist 0.3.1\n✔ The default environment has been installed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json,hashlib\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('scientific-judgment.json'); x=json.loads(p.read_text()); b=Path(x['report']['path']).read_bytes(); x['report']['sha256']=hashlib.sha256(b).hexdigest(); p.write_text(json.dumps(x,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\n\\\"\"'$STAMPED_ASSESSMENT_PYTHON\" \"$STAMPED_SCIENTIFIC_JUDGMENT_VALIDATOR\" validate scientific-judgment.json --workspace \"$STAMPED_JUDGE_OUTPUT\" --delivery-manifest \"$STAMPED_DELIVERY_MANIFEST\" > commands/scientific-validate.stdout 2> commands/scientific-validate.stderr; echo $? > commands/scientific-validate.exit; cat commands/scientific-validate.stdout; cat commands/scientific-validate.stderr\ncat > commands/session-ledger.md <<'\"'EOF'\n# Assessment command ledger\n\nAll commands ran with the launcher-provided \"'`GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0`, `annex.merge-annex-branches=false`, and `annex.alwayscommit=false` inherited.\n\n## Persisted command outputs\n\n- `runner-check.*`: required frozen runner `check` before any probe or response action.\n- `probes.*`: frozen probe run on the operational copy; raw result is `../probes.json`.\n- `response-template.*`, `response-stamp.*`, `response-set-*.{stdout,stderr,exit}`, `response-table.*`, `response-encode.*`, `response-validate.*`: frozen runner response actions. `apply-responses.stderr` retains the initial failed orchestration traceback; `apply-responses.exit` retains its final status.\n- `scientific-validate.*`: required scientific record validator.\n- `check-integrity.*`: final inspection-copy byte/link comparison. It reports zero non-permitted differences and records the permitted annex database metadata differences. The final Git status is `final-git-status.*`.\n- Helper source used to orchestrate response setting and integrity comparison is preserved as `apply_responses.py` and `check-integrity.py`.\n\n## Failed or revised attempts\n\n- An initial response-setting orchestration stopped before setting answers because a tuple was passed where an argument string was expected; it made no target change. The traceback and status are retained in `apply-responses.stderr` and `.exit`. The corrected orchestration used the frozen response action and passed response validation.\n- The first scientific-record construction had a missing excerpt anchor and raised `ValueError`; no record was written by that attempt. The corrected record was validated. The exception was returned by the tool session; see this ledger'\"'s session note.\n- The first three exploratory integrity-comparison revisions falsely counted representation differences (manifest path fields, external capture resources, and symlink metadata) as mismatches. Their outputs were returned in the session; the final comparator normalizes those capture-specific representations and reports zero non-permitted differences. None of these checks modified the target.\n\n## Exploratory inspection\n\nInitial read-only shell inspections and their stdout/stderr were returned in the assessment tool session rather than redirected to individual files. The final evidence and relevant command outputs are summarized in \"'`../report.md`, `../probes.json`, `check-integrity.stdout`, and the frozen runner records above. The broad initial procedure dump exposed coordinator-retained identifiers and commit metadata; these were not used. No other workers'\"' scientific outputs or prior judgments were opened or used.\nEOF\n\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
